Mike Quinn complains that nethack doesn't tell him which 'd' is his dog.
Well, nethack does let you know which monsters are your pets, but you
have to take advantage of these things.  You _do_ know what your pet
looks like.  If not, you wouldn't stop from hitting it.

I have 3 ways to keep from wasting a turn in discovering which is your pet:

1) play a wizard.  Then you always get a feline.  :-)
2) Use the "/" command before each move.  Since your complaint was
   that you should know which is your pet, just "/" it, if it says the
   monster is tame, don't hit it.  "/" takes no game time.
3) Use a color display.  Normal domestic pets get displayed as white,
   other animals are shown in other colors (yellow, for example).
   Doesn't help you if you tame a jackal, though.
4) Set "!safepet".  Then it won't cost you a move -- it'll just ask
   if you really want to go that way, you say no and go somewhere else.

Before you flame, yeah, it would be nice if you could tell more easily.
At least between (2) and (4), you have a something almost as nice
already.

